In</span> <span data-s=\"57\" data-w=\"1\">the</span> <span data-s=\"57\" data-w=\"2\">table</span> <span data-s=\"57\" data-w=\"3\">above,</span> <span data-s=\"57\" data-w=\"4\">three</span> <span data-s=\"57\" data-w=\"5\">of</span> <span data-s=\"57\" data-w=\"6\">five</span> <span data-s=\"57\" data-w=\"7\">offers</span> <span data-s=\"57\" data-w=\"8\">are</span> <span data-s=\"57\" data-w=\"9\">accepted</span> <span data-s=\"57\" data-w=\"10\">(60%).</span> <span data-s=\"58\" data-w=\"0\">A</span> <span data-s=\"58\" data-w=\"1\">baseline</span> <span data-s=\"58\" data-w=\"2\">that</span> <span data-s=\"58\" data-w=\"3\">always</span> <span data-s=\"58\" data-w=\"4\">predicts</span> <span data-s=\"58\" data-w=\"5\">\"accepted\"</span> <span data-s=\"58\" data-w=\"6\">is</span> <span data-s=\"58\" data-w=\"7\">right</span> <span data-s=\"58\" data-w=\"8\">60%</span> <span data-s=\"58\" data-w=\"9\">of</span> <span data-s=\"58\" data-w=\"10\">the</span> <span data-s=\"58\" data-w=\"11\">time.</span> <span data-s=\"59\" data-w=\"0\">Any</span> <span data-s=\"59\" data-w=\"1\">classifier</span> <span data-s=\"59\" data-w=\"2\">you</span> <span data-s=\"59\" data-w=\"3\">build</span> <span data-s=\"59\" data-w=\"4\">on</span> <span data-s=\"59\" data-w=\"5\">this</span> <span data-s=\"59\" data-w=\"6\">table</span> <span data-s=\"59\" data-w=\"7\">must</span> <span data-s=\"59\" data-w=\"8\">beat</span> <span data-s=\"59\" data-w=\"9\">60%,</span> <span data-s=\"59\" data-w=\"10\">measured</span> <span data-s=\"59\" data-w=\"11\">on</span> <span data-s=\"59\" data-w=\"12\">rows</span> <span data-s=\"59\" data-w=\"13\">it</span> <span data-s=\"59\" data-w=\"14\">did</span> <span data-s=\"59\" data-w=\"15\">not</span> <span data-s=\"59\" data-w=\"16\">train</span> <span data-s=\"59\" data-w=\"17\">on.</span></p>\n<p><strong><span data-s=\"60\" data-w=\"0\">Common</span> <span data-s=\"60\" data-w=\"1\">mistakes</span></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><span data-s=\"61\" data-w=\"0\">Scoring</span> <span data-s=\"61\" data-w=\"1\">a</span> <span data-s=\"61\" data-w=\"2\">model</span> <span data-s=\"61\" data-w=\"3\">on</span> <span data-s=\"61\" data-w=\"4\">its</span> <span data-s=\"61\" data-w=\"5\">training</span> <span data-s=\"61\" data-w=\"6\">data,</span> <span data-s=\"61\" data-w=\"7\">and</span> <span data-s=\"61\" data-w=\"8\">then</span> <span data-s=\"61\" data-w=\"9\">being</span> <span data-s=\"61\" data-w=\"10\">surprised</span> <span data-s=\"61\" data-w=\"11\">in</span> <span data-s=\"61\" data-w=\"12\">production.</span></li>\n<li><span data-s=\"62\" data-w=\"0\">Scaling</span> <span data-s=\"62\" data-w=\"1\">or</span> <span data-s=\"62\" data-w=\"2\">cleaning</span> <span data-s=\"62\" data-w=\"3\">the</span> <span data-s=\"62\" data-w=\"4\">whole</span> <span data-s=\"62\" data-w=\"5\">dataset</span> <span data-s=\"62\" data-w=\"6\">before</span> <span data-s=\"62\" data-w=\"7\">splitting</span> <span data-s=\"62\" data-w=\"8\">it</span> <span data-s=\"62\" data-w=\"9\">(leakage).</span></li>\n<li><span data-s=\"63\" data-w=\"0\">Random-splitting</span> <span data-s=\"63\" data-w=\"1\">time-ordered</span> <span data-s=\"63\" data-w=\"2\">data.</span></li>\n<li><span data-s=\"64\" data-w=\"0\">Skipping</span> <span data-s=\"64\" data-w=\"1\">the</span> <span data-s=\"64\" data-w=\"2\">baseline.</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Check yourself</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>In the offers table, what are m and n, and what is x^(3)?</li>\n<li>What is the difference between a parameter and a hyperparameter? Give an example of each.</li>\n<li>Why must a test set be used only once, at the end?</li>\n<li>Give an example of leakage in a loan model.</li>\n</ul>\n<details class=\"answers\"><summary>Show answers</summary><p> (1) m = 5, n = 3, x^(3) = [5000, 24, 780]. (2) A parameter is learned (a weight w); a hyperparameter is chosen by you (the learning rate). (3) If you tune on it, it stops being unseen data and the score becomes too optimistic. (4) Using \"days in collections\" to predict default: you only know it after the default has started.</p></details>\n<p><strong>Go deeper:</strong> Google's <a href=\"https://developers.google.com/machine-learning/guides/rules-of-ml\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Rules of Machine Learning</a> (practical, written by engineers) · the scikit-learn pages on <a href=\"https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/cross_validation.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">cross-validation</a> and <a href=\"https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/preprocessing.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">preprocessing</a> · <em>An Introduction to Statistical Learning</em>, <a href=\"https://www.statlearning.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">free book</a>.</p>\n"}